  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="commodity_treacle_cb1b349d7f8c91cd0e240c8ddeb6e96a0c36a848c8e1125b0c872030099cbf8a920">
    <crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>treacle, uncrystallized syrup produced in the process of refining sugar (OED s.v. treacle II.4.a) | (treakle voc’ Flaunders treakle) | receptacle for treacle | treacle, uncrystallized syrup produced in the process of refining sugar (OED s.v. treacle II.4.a), used medically (MED s.v. triacle n.) | treacle, uncrystallized syrup produced in the process of refining sugar (OED s.v. treacle II.4.a), used medicinally 497; 508; | treacle, originally a kind of salve, composed of many ingredients, formerly in repute as an alexipharmic against and antidote to venomous bites, poisons generally, and malignant diseases (medical); later uncrystallized syrup produced in the process of refining sugar (OED s.v. treacle 1, 4) | a salve, made of many ingredients, for treating animals (OED s.v. treacle n. 1a) | medicinal compound, originally a kind of salve, composed of many ingredients, formerly in repute as an alexipharmic against and antidote to venomous bites, poisons generally, and malignant diseases (OED s.v. treacle n. 1a), here manufactured in Flanders | a container for (sugary) treacle as an article of commerce</crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>
    <crm:P2_has_type rdf:resource="http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object"/>
  </rdf:Description>
